From d6ab94b80a118dd80fb5d26ee3882f046f8a820e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kebab-port <kebab-port@local>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 10:57:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: samsung-amb655x: set dsc_slice_per_pkt=2 from
 stock dtbo

The stock dtbo node qcom,mdss_dsi_oplus20828samsung_amb655x_1080_2400_cmd
declares qcom,mdss-dsc-slice-per-pkt = <2>. msm derives bytes_per_pkt and
pkt_per_line from mipi_dsi_device.dsc_slice_per_pkt; leaving the field at 0
makes the host pack one slice per packet, which this panel cannot decode, so
the internal panel stays black while the rest of the pipeline reports frames.
Set it to the value the vendor device tree requires.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-amb655x.c | 12 +++++++-----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-amb655x.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-amb655x.c
index 64ec7df3b..02551a459 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-amb655x.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-amb655x.c
@@ -443,12 +443,14 @@ static int samsung_amb655x_probe(struct mipi_dsi_device *dsi)
 	ctx->dsc.block_pred_enable = true;
 
 	/*
-	 * dsi->dsc_slice_per_pkt is left at 0, which msm treats as 1. The
-	 * original TODO asked for 2, but 1 is what the known-good 6.8 build
-	 * used, since the field did not exist then. If the panel lights up
-	 * but shows garbage or tearing, setting this to 2 is the first thing
-	 * to try.
+	 * The stock dtbo node for this exact panel
+	 * (qcom,mdss_dsi_oplus20828samsung_amb655x_1080_2400_cmd) declares
+	 * qcom,mdss-dsc-slice-per-pkt = <2>. msm derives both bytes_per_pkt and
+	 * pkt_per_line from this field; leaving it at 0 makes the host pack one
+	 * slice per packet, which the panel cannot decode. That mismatch keeps
+	 * the display black even though the DSI link itself is running.
 	 */
+	dsi->dsc_slice_per_pkt = 2;
 
 	ret = mipi_dsi_attach(dsi);
 	if (ret < 0) {
-- 
2.47.3

